.\" Generated by "sysml-mcp -man"; edit the description in the command's usage.go.
.TH SYSML-MCP 1 "2026-08-30" "OpenSysML" "OpenSysML Manual"
.SH NAME
sysml\-mcp \- Model Context Protocol server for SysML v2 and KerML
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysml\-mcp
[options]
.br
.B sysml\-mcp
\-http ADDR [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
sysml\-mcp serves OpenSysML to coding agents over the Model Context Protocol,
as tools an agent calls: the language server's diagnostics, navigation,
editing and rendering over the model documents under the workspace root; the
runtime's one\-shot parsing, evaluation, instantiation, execution,
verification, querying and conversion; and named REPL sessions whose
declarations, instances and runs persist across calls; the protocol is spoken
over stdin/stdout, so an agent host starts this server rather than a shell, or
over Streamable HTTP at the address \-http names.
.PP
The documents under the root are managed as one workspace, so a declaration in
one resolves against the others, and the standard library is the copy embedded
in this binary unless OPENSYSML_LIBRARY_PATH names another.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-allow\-origin " string"
Origins, comma\-separated as scheme://host[:port], granted cross\-origin
access to the HTTP transport (the CORS headers and preflight answer a browser
needs); loopback origins and requests with no Origin header are admitted
without a grant, any other origin is refused
.TP
.BI \-cache\-size " int"
Maximum number of parsed models the runtime tools hold; at least 1. The
default is 100.
.TP
.B \-h
Show this help (shorthand)
.TP
.B \-help
Show this help and exit
.TP
.BI \-http " string"
Serve over Streamable HTTP at the path /mcp of this address instead of
stdin/stdout, as host:port or a port alone, which binds loopback; every client
shares the one workspace, runtime cache and set of REPL sessions. An address
other machines reach is served only with a bearer token (\-token\-file,
\-token or OPENSYSML_MCP_TOKEN)
.TP
.BI \-log\-level " string"
Lowest level logged to stderr: debug, info, warn or error. The default is
warn.
.TP
.B \-man
Write this command's manual page, in roff, to stdout and exit
.TP
.B \-no\-record\-cache
Parse every document and hold it loaded, reading no interface record from the
record cache and writing none; default off, or OPENSYSML_RECORD_CACHE=0
.TP
.B \-print\-config
Write the configuration block declaring this server to an agent host \(em
opencode, claude\-code, cursor, codex, vscode, gemini, devin \(em to stdout
and exit; alone, list the hosts
.TP
.BI \-print\-config\-command " string"
Command the \-print\-config block names instead of this binary's absolute
path, such as sysml\-mcp when it is on PATH
.TP
.B \-print\-config\-npx
Make the \-print\-config block start the server as npx \-y
@openmbee/sysml\-mcp, which npm installs on first use, instead of naming this
binary
.TP
.BI \-root " string"
Workspace folder whose model documents the server indexes and edits; default
the current directory, which an agent host sets to the project. The default is
\&..
.TP
.B \-stdio
Serve over stdin/stdout (the default transport; accepted for hosts that name
it; not with \-http)
.TP
.B \-strict
Serve strict conformance from the start: notation no pinned SysML v2
production admits is an error
.TP
.BI \-tls\-cert " string"
TLS certificate file for the HTTP transport; with \-tls\-key, the transport
serves https
.TP
.BI \-tls\-key " string"
TLS private key file for the HTTP transport
.TP
.BI \-token " string"
The bearer token itself, for a shell whose command line is private;
\-token\-file keeps it out of the process list, and OPENSYSML_MCP_TOKEN is
read when neither flag names one
.TP
.BI \-token\-file " string"
File holding the bearer token every HTTP request must carry as Authorization:
Bearer TOKEN (a trailing line break is not part of it); required for an
address other machines reach, enforced on loopback too when given
.TP
.BI \-tools " string"
Tool groups to serve, comma\-separated: lsp (diagnostics, navigation, editing,
rendering), runtime (one\-shot evaluation, execution, verification,
conversion), session (persistent REPL sessions); default all. The default is
all.
.TP
.B \-v
Show version (shorthand)
.TP
.B \-version
Show version information
.SH STARTING THE SERVER
.RS 2
.nf
# What an agent host runs, in the project directory
sysml\-mcp
# Serve the models under another folder
sysml\-mcp \-root models
# Serve without persistent sessions
sysml\-mcp \-tools lsp,runtime
.fi
.RE
.PP
An agent host declares the server in its configuration, as {"mcp": {"sysml":
{"type": "local", "command": ["sysml\-mcp"]}}} in OpenCode's opencode.json,
and starts it with the project as the working directory.
.SH TRANSPORTS
Without \-http the protocol is spoken over stdin and stdout: the host starts
the server, which serves that one client and exits when the stream closes.
With \-http the server is started once and serves every client that connects
to its address over the Streamable HTTP transport, at the path /mcp, until it
is told to stop with SIGINT or SIGTERM; stopping closes the sessions and waits
up to 30 seconds for the connections to drain. The clients share one
workspace, one runtime cache and one set of REPL sessions, so a session_* name
opened by one is the session every other sees under that name.
.PP
.RS 2
.nf
sysml\-mcp \-http 8765  # Serve http://localhost:8765/mcp to this machine
# Serve every interface over https to clients that hold the token
sysml\-mcp \-http 0.0.0.0:8765 \-token\-file mcp.token \-tls\-cert \e
    server.crt \-tls\-key server.key
# Answer one browser origin besides loopback
sysml\-mcp \-http 0.0.0.0:8765 \-token\-file mcp.token \-allow\-origin \e
    https://agents.example.org
.fi
.RE
.PP
An address with no host, or a port alone, binds loopback, which only this
machine reaches, and is served as it is. Any other address is served only with
a bearer token, named by \-token\-file, \-token or OPENSYSML_MCP_TOKEN: the
server is an OAuth 2.1 resource server in the minimal form, with one token
issued by whoever runs it, so every request must carry Authorization: Bearer
TOKEN, and one that does not is refused with 401 and a WWW\-Authenticate
challenge naming the resource metadata at
/.well\-known/oauth\-protected\-resource/mcp. Starting on such an address with
no token is refused. A token given for a loopback address is enforced the same
way. The token is letters, digits and \-._~+/ (RFC 6750), is never logged, and
is best generated, as by openssl rand \-base64 32, and kept in a file only the
server's user reads. \-tls\-cert and \-tls\-key, both given, serve https,
which a token sent over a network needs; one without the other is refused.
.PP
A request is answered when its Origin header is absent, names a loopback
origin (localhost, 127.0.0.0/8 or ::1 over any scheme and port) or names an
origin listed in \-allow\-origin exactly; any other origin is refused with
403, which keeps a page on another site from reaching the server through a DNS
name rebound to this machine. The wildcard origin is not accepted. A request
whose MCP\-Protocol\-Version header names a version the server does not speak
is refused with 400.
.SH CONFIGURING A HOST
\-print\-config writes the block a host reads, naming this binary by its
absolute path so the host finds it wherever it was installed;
\-print\-config\-command names another command instead, such as sysml\-mcp
when it is on PATH, and \-print\-config\-npx names npx \-y
@openmbee/sysml\-mcp, which installs the release binary for the host's
platform from npm on first use, so a machine with Node needs nothing else.
With \-http (and \-tls\-cert for https) the block names the URL of a server
already serving that address instead, and with its token (\-token\-file,
\-token or OPENSYSML_MCP_TOKEN) the Authorization header the host sends,
written in clear, so such a block belongs in a file the host reads privately,
not in version control; every host reads the URL form. The hosts, with the
file each reads, are opencode (opencode.json), claude\-code (.mcp.json),
cursor (.cursor/mcp.json), codex (~/.codex/config.toml), vscode
(.vscode/mcp.json), gemini (.gemini/settings.json), devin (Customize > MCPs >
Add custom MCP).
.PP
.RS 2
.nf
# List the hosts
sysml\-mcp \-print\-config
# The mcp block of opencode.json
sysml\-mcp \-print\-config opencode
# Append the [mcp_servers.sysml] table
sysml\-mcp \-print\-config codex >> ~/.codex/config.toml
# A block that finds the server on PATH
sysml\-mcp \-print\-config cursor \-print\-config\-command sysml\-mcp
# A block that runs the server from npm
sysml\-mcp \-print\-config vscode \-print\-config\-npx
# A block reaching http://localhost:8765/mcp
sysml\-mcp \-print\-config vscode \-http 8765
# A block reaching a remote server with its token
sysml\-mcp \-print\-config cursor \-http models.example.org:8443 \e
    \-tls\-cert server.crt \-tls\-key server.key \-token\-file mcp.token
.fi
.RE
.SH TOOLS
The tools, by the group that serves them (\-tools), each with the sysml\-grpc
RPC or sysml flag it stands for. The tool_catalog tool answers this list to
the client, narrowed to the groups served.
.TP
.B tool_catalog
every group: List the tools this server serves, each with the RPC or sysml
flag it stands for.
.TP
.B apply_model_edit
lsp: Edit a model by operations on its elements (setValue, rename, addMember,
delete, move, ...) and answer the text edits; write them with apply.
.TP
.B close_document
lsp: Release a document held open by open_document; the server reads the file
on disk again.
.TP
.B code_actions
lsp: List the quick fixes and refactorings available for a range of a
document, each with its edits.
.TP
.B completion
lsp: Propose completions at a position: keywords, names in scope and members
of the accessed type.
.TP
.B definition
lsp: Find where the name at a position is declared.
.TP
.B document_symbols
lsp: Outline a document: the elements it declares, nested as they are owned.
.TP
.B documents
lsp: List the document definitions declared across the workspace.
.TP
.B format
lsp: Format a document, or a range of it, in the canonical style; write the
file with apply.
.TP
.B hover
lsp: Explain the element at a position: kind, qualified name, type, value and
documentation.
.TP
.B inlay_hints
lsp: List the inferred types and values an editor would show inline for a
document or range.
.TP
.B open_document
lsp: Hold a document open with the given text, analyzed instead of the file on
disk.
.TP
.B references
lsp: Find every place in the workspace that refers to the element at a
position.
.TP
.B rename
lsp: Rename the element at a position everywhere in the workspace; write the
files with apply.
.TP
.B render_document
lsp: Render a document definition of the workspace to Markdown, its queries
evaluated and its diagrams embedded.
.TP
.B render_view
lsp: Render a declared view or pseudo\-view of a workspace document as
Mermaid, dot, PlantUML, D2, text or a table.
.TP
.B signature_help
lsp: Describe the invocation enclosing a position: its parameters and the
active one.
.TP
.B update_document
lsp: Replace the text of a document held open by open_document and answer the
diagnostics of the new text.
.TP
.B views
lsp: List the views a document declares and the pseudo\-views render_view can
draw of it.
.TP
.B workspace_diagnostics
lsp: List the errors, warnings and hints of one workspace document or of the
whole workspace.
.TP
.B workspace_info
lsp: Describe the workspace root and the documents it holds, with their
diagnostic counts.
.TP
.B workspace_symbols
lsp: Search the workspace's declared elements by name substring.
.TP
.B apply_edits
runtime: Apply workspace edits to a parsed model and answer the edited
documents (rpc ApplyEdits).
.TP
.B compare_results
runtime: Run the configurations a SysML v1 tool's results index and table the
tool's distributions beside the runs' (rpc CompareResults, sysml
\-compare\-results).
.TP
.B convert
runtime: Convert a model between the textual notation, JSON, RDF and XMI (rpc
Convert, sysml \-convert, sysml \-from, sysml \-id).
.TP
.B diagnostics
runtime: Report every diagnostic of a parsed model, as sysml \-validate does
(rpc GetDiagnostics, sysml \-validate, sysml \-disable\-lint, sysml
\-enable\-lint).
.TP
.B explain_diagnostic
runtime: Explain a diagnostic code, or list every code with its summary (sysml
\-explain).
.TP
.B evaluate
runtime: Evaluate an expression against a parsed model (rpc Evaluate, sysml
\-eval).
.TP
.B evaluate_calc
runtime: Evaluate a calculation definition or usage (rpc EvaluateCalc, sysml
\-calc).
.TP
.B execute_action
runtime: Execute an action with bound inputs and report its outputs (rpc
ExecuteAction, sysml \-action, sysml \-schedule, sysml \-advance, sysml
\-seed, sysml \-draws, sysml \-clock\-step).
.TP
.B execute_state
runtime: Run a state machine over a sequence of events and report the trace
(rpc ExecuteState, sysml \-state).
.TP
.B export_graphs
runtime: Export the lowered action and state graphs of a model (rpc
ExportGraphs, sysml \-graphs).
.TP
.B import_data
runtime: Set the feature values a CSV, TSV, JSON or JSON Lines file assigns,
one row per element (rpc ImportData, sysml \-import, sysml \-import\-as, sysml
\-import\-map, sysml \-import\-format, sysml \-import\-dry\-run).
.TP
.B instantiate
runtime: Instantiate a definition or usage and report the object's feature
values (rpc Instantiate, sysml \-instantiate).
.TP
.B list_engines
runtime: List the analysis engines and whether each is ready (rpc ListEngines,
sysml \-engines, sysml \-probe).
.TP
.B migrate
runtime: Migrate a SysML v1 model to SysML v2 and report what moved (rpc
Migrate, sysml \-migrate, sysml \-migration\-report, sysml
\-migration\-results, sysml \-layout, sysml \-image\-base\-url).
.TP
.B parse
runtime: Parse files or inline sources and answer the roots, diagnostics and a
model hash (rpc ParseFile, rpc ParseSources, sysml \-strict).
.TP
.B query
runtime: Run an OSLC query against a parsed model (rpc Query, sysml \-query).
.TP
.B render_model_document
runtime: Render a document definition as Markdown or HTML (rpc RenderDocument,
sysml \-render\-document, sysml \-doc\-form).
.TP
.B record_run
runtime: Run an analysis case and record the runs into the model as
AnalysisRecords declarations (rpc RecordRun, sysml \-record\-run, sysml
\-record\-into).
.TP
.B render_model_view
runtime: Render a view as its nodes, edges and compartments (rpc RenderView,
sysml \-render, sysml \-render\-ports, sysml \-render\-show, sysml
\-render\-depth).
.TP
.B check_behavior
runtime: Search every schedule of an action or state machine for violated
properties, deadlocks, failures and divergent values (rpc CheckBehavior, sysml
\-check\-property, sysml \-check\-diverge, sysml \-check\-input, sysml
\-check\-assume, sysml \-check\-witness, sysml \-check\-depth, sysml
\-check\-states, sysml \-check\-unroll, sysml \-check\-timeout).
.TP
.B run_analysis
runtime: Run an analysis case and report its result (rpc RunAnalysis, sysml
\-analysis, sysml \-engine, sysml \-tool\-dry\-run).
.TP
.B run_document_query
runtime: Run a document query definition and report its rows (rpc
RunDocumentQuery, sysml \-run\-query).
.TP
.B run_runs
runtime: Run an action or a Monte Carlo case repeatedly and table what the
runs observed (rpc RunRuns, sysml \-runs, sysml \-observe).
.TP
.B run_sweep
runtime: Run an analysis case over ranges of its parameters (rpc RunSweep,
sysml \-sweep, sysml \-samples).
.TP
.B self_check
runtime: Apply the reflective SysMLValidation constraints to every element of
a model (rpc SelfCheck, sysml \-self\-check, sysml \-self\-check\-package).
.TP
.B server_info
runtime: Report the service version and the capabilities it serves (rpc
GetServerInfo).
.TP
.B symbol
runtime: Describe one element of a parsed model (rpc GetSymbol).
.TP
.B validate_instance
runtime: Validate an instantiated object against its definition, as sysml
\-validate=<object> does (rpc ValidateInstance).
.TP
.B verify_constraint
runtime: Verify a constraint and answer the verdict (rpc VerifyConstraint,
sysml \-constraint).
.TP
.B verify_requirement
runtime: Verify a requirement and answer the verdict (rpc VerifyRequirement,
sysml \-requirement).
.TP
.B verify_satisfaction
runtime: Verify a satisfy relationship and answer the verdict (rpc
VerifySatisfaction, sysml \-satisfy).
.TP
.B advance
session: Advance the debugged state machine's clock by a duration, firing the
timed transitions due.
.TP
.B check
session: Check with the SMT solver whether an element's constraints are
satisfiable.
.TP
.B configure
session: Choose variant selections for a variation model, or enumerate every
valid configuration.
.TP
.B debug_breakpoints
session: List, set or clear the breakpoints of the debugged action.
.TP
.B debug_continue
session: Run the debugged action or state machine on to its next breakpoint or
its end.
.TP
.B debug_current
session: Report the debugger's state: the action's tokens and breakpoints, or
the machine's state, clock and event queue.
.TP
.B debug_start
session: Start debugging an action or a state machine by qualified name.
.TP
.B debug_step
session: Step the debugged action or state machine once.
.TP
.B debug_stop
session: Stop debugging and discard the debugged executors.
.TP
.B explain
session: Explain why an element's constraints are unsatisfiable, naming the
conflicting ones.
.TP
.B features
session: List a runtime instance's feature values, with its object graph.
.TP
.B instances
session: List the runtime instances the session holds.
.TP
.B optimize
session: Optimize an analysis case's objective with the solver and answer the
optimum.
.TP
.B render_run
session: Render a run's trace as a timeline or a sequence diagram.
.TP
.B repl_command
session: Run one % meta command of the REPL and answer its output lines.
.TP
.B runs
session: Run an action repeatedly, or a Monte Carlo case, and table the
outcomes.
.TP
.B send
session: Send a signal to the debugged state machine.
.TP
.B session_clear
session: Clear a session's declarations, instances and debuggers.
.TP
.B session_close
session: Close an open REPL session.
.TP
.B session_eval
session: Evaluate an expression in a session and answer its value.
.TP
.B session_list
session: List the open REPL sessions.
.TP
.B session_load
session: Load model files under the workspace root into a session and answer
the diagnostics.
.TP
.B session_open
session: Open a REPL session over a workspace and answer its id.
.TP
.B session_print
session: Print a session's declarations back as SysML notation.
.TP
.B session_run
session: Run an action, state machine, calculation or analysis case in a
session and answer the verdict.
.TP
.B session_save
session: Preview a session's model as a file under the workspace root, or
write it with apply.
.TP
.B session_submit
session: Submit declarations to a session and answer what was declared and the
diagnostics.
.TP
.B solve
session: Synthesize feature values satisfying an element's constraints with
the solver.
.TP
.B sweep
session: Sweep a calculation over a range or sampled values and table the
results.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The status reports how the session ended:
.TP
.B 0
The protocol was served to its end: the client closed the stream, or the
process was told to stop.
.TP
.B 1
The server could not start, as when the \-http address is in use, or the
session ended in a protocol error.
.TP
.B 2
The command line could not be acted on.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_LIBRARY_PATH
Directory to load the SysML/KerML standard library from, instead of the copy
embedded in the binary.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_LIBRARY_ROOTS
Directories, separated as PATH is, to look for installed projects under when a
loaded file belongs to a project (a directory holding .project.json), besides
the project's own well\-known library directory (.sysand/lib).
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_STEPS
Expression evaluations one run may spend before it is reported as a runaway.
Default 10000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_ACTION_STEPS
Token\-flow steps one action run may perform. Default 1000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_EVENTS
Events one state machine run may dispatch. Default 1000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_DO_STEPS
Do actions one state machine run may perform. Default 5000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_ELEMENTS
Collection elements one evaluation may hold, which bounds the memory a run
holds rather than the work it does. Default 1000000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_CALC_DEPTH
Nested calc invocations one run may hold on the stack, which is what a
recursion spends. Default 10000, ceiling 25000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_SWEEP_RUNS
Runs one parameter sweep or sample may make, each a whole analysis or calc run
of its own with its own budgets. Default 1000.
.TP
.B OPENSYSML_MAX_INTEGER_BITS
Bits the magnitude of one Integer a run computes may take; Integers are
otherwise unbounded, and a result past it, such as a large power, is refused
before it is computed. At least 64, so every machine\-word Integer fits;
default 1048576.
.PP
Each variable above also answers to its legacy SYSML_\-prefixed name
(SYSML_MAX_STEPS for OPENSYSML_MAX_STEPS, and so on), which remains accepted.
When both are set and the OPENSYSML_ value is non\-empty, the OPENSYSML_ value
wins; setting only the legacy name prints a one\-time deprecation warning on
standard error.
.PP
A budget bounds one run \(em one evaluation, one instantiation, one calc
invocation, one action, one state machine \(em not a whole session, so a long
session of small operations never exhausts one. A run started inside another
shares the outer run's budget.
